WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.767
This project combines joins with skills from earlier
modules The common

00:00:05.793 --> 00:00:10.438
table expression creates a patient timeline by
stacking admissions lab tests and

00:00:10.451 --> 00:00:15.374
prescriptions with UNION ALL Each source is
transformed into the same four-column

00:00:15.388 --> 00:00:21.717
event structure patient ID date event type and event
details After

00:00:21.743 --> 00:00:25.243
that event stream is created we join it to patients
using patient

00:00:25.269 --> 00:00:30.466
ID so the timeline includes the patient name Run the
query and

00:00:30.492 --> 00:00:35.350
inspect one patient across several dates You should
see different event types

00:00:35.377 --> 00:00:40.558
ordered into a single history The important join
idea is that we

00:00:40.585 --> 00:00:43.637
first create a source at a clear grain one row per
event

00:00:43.874 --> 00:00:48.719
and then enrich those events with patient data This
is a useful

00:00:48.746 --> 00:00:54.298
pattern for audit histories customer journeys
student activity timelines and operational event

00:00:54.311 --> 00:00:54.890
streams
